	Thanks to all!

	I'm not sure exactly what fixed it, but I put "export
DTNONETWORK=true" at the end of my .dtprofile, logged in in failsafe mode,
logged  back in in normal mode, and it works fine now.

	This information came from John Lanier:

1. Assure that you have the appropriate value set in /etc/rc.config:

--> rcmgr get XLOGIN
cde

2.    Use the "Failsafe" session option on the login screen to 
	allow you to login with just mwm and an xterm. 

Edit your $HOME/.dtprofile and add the following line at the end:

	export DTNONETWORK=true

	Now try and login to a normal CDE session.  If successful, 
	this may represent a transient network problem.  If not, 
	then the network needs to be investigated further.


-denise


