Hello Admin Wizards,

Pat O`Brien  (thank you!) pointed me to a problem I did not realize.

In my case, I replaced a small Backup raid (6x2GB on 130-630) with a 
slightly bigger one (12x2 GB on 120-630), Raid 5.

Now if a disk fails, everything is fine and the controller will replace 
it from the set of hot spares on 110-410.
BUT if a controller port fails - and even though I use dual redundant 
HSZ 40s, the risk is to be considered - TWO disks will fail, leaving the 
backup set useless.
Thus I am considering various options now - if anyone here is familiar 
with the HSZ 40s, is it possible to create two raid sets (120-620 and 
130-630) and stripe the two of them together on controller level?
I dont have lsm on my system - looking for a reliable solution on 
controller level.

would be thankful for hints in that case.
CW

---------- Original Summary below: -----------------------

thanks to Peter Gergen, Tom Swigg and Michael Polnick who pointed me
that the disk needs to be labeled too, since it still had the old label
from the 10 GB config.

disklabel -z /dev/rz18
disklabel -wr -t advfs /dev/rz18

did the job.

Thanks for the accurate and FAST help!

CW
-------------------------------------------------------------
