Several people suggested that one of the options buried in the GUI 
was to switch back to the text console.  I eventually found it, I'll 
paste the directions Travis Ostachuk sent me:

At 12:45 PM -0400 10/15/03, Osatchuk, Trevor wrote:
>1.  After power up press F2 to enter setup
>2.  Select CMOS setup
>3.  Press F6 to enter advanced
>4.  Tab to Console Selection
>5.  Select Digital Unix Console (SRM)
>6.  Press F10 key twice
>7.  Press Enter
>8.  Power Cycle.

Once I told did the power cycle the system booted up into Tru64 
without any problems.  (I think the GUI Console can't recognize UNIX 
partitions, so that's why I though the HD had crashed).

thanks for the help,
James
