Summary:

Thanks to everyone who replied. I tried Robert Schueler's approach fi=
rst and
it worked.=20

He said: "Apply the attached patch to your cyrus-sasl-Sources. It see=
ms to
be only necessary for Tru64 5.1a and before." Since it was a one line
configure file edit, I actually did this change by hand rather than b=
y
applying the patch. Worked great.

The patch file is in plain text below.








PATCH FILE CONTENTS:
*** configure.orig=09Wed Jul  2 14:29:20 2003
--- configure=09Wed Jul  2 14:29:40 2003
***************
*** 6678,6684 ****
  EOF
  if { (eval echo configure:6680: \"$ac_link\") 1>&5; (eval $ac_link)=
 2>&5;
} && test -s conftest${ac_exeext}; then
    rm -rf conftest*
!   eval "ac_cv_func_getnameinfo=3Dyes"
  else
    echo "configure: failed program was:" >&5
    cat conftest.$ac_ext >&5
--- 6678,6684 ----
  EOF
  if { (eval echo configure:6680: \"$ac_link\") 1>&5; (eval $ac_link)=
 2>&5;
} && test -s conftest${ac_exeext}; then
    rm -rf conftest*
!   eval "ac_cv_func_getnameinfo=3Dno"
  else
    echo "configure: failed program was:" >&5
    cat conftest.$ac_ext >&5


