Hi,

the problem was as suggested an autonegotiation issue. 
Thanks for the input by Werner Rost(werner.rost@zfboge.com) 
and Russ, Vernon J. (vjruss@tva.gov). Werner pointed out 
that he in general does not use autonegotiation
1. im Konsolmodus:      set ewa0_mode ...
2. in /etc/rc.config:   IFCONFIG_0="10.3.7.149 netmask 
255.255.252.0 speed  200"	(i.e. 100FD)
Vernon gave some general hints
I suggest you look at:
  netstat -i    for errors.
  netstat -r    to be sure your routing table is correct. 
You might want to flush the routing table.
  arp -a    to be sure the arp cache is correct.  You might 
want to flush arp cache.

I finally set the speed in the running system with
ifconfig tu0 speed 200 on all involved systems and the 
errors didn't appear anymore.

Unfortunately I didn't find yet means how to check the 
actual speed of the NIC. I could it only check indirectly 
when I changed the switch port speed to the same value and 
it worked. Werner gave the hint to look into 
/var/adm/messages. But here the information is only provided 
after Booting. This helped to find the current settings but 
is not appropriate if one makes changes in the running system.

Regards

Otto


