I also learned from HP that there is no timeout value associated with an ICMP redirect route entry in the route table ("D" flag).  They never expire.  The only way they leave is if there is a modified redirect or thy are manually deleted.

However, in patch build 24 (patchkit 6 for 5.1A, patchkit 3 for 5.1B), there is a kernel configuration setting added to enable this.  "icmp_redirect_timeout" will be added to the inet stanza of the sysconfigtab file.  You can give it a value in seconds of when you want "stale" ICMP redirect entries to drop off the route table. 

